{"name":"Nyanza","hex":"#e9ffdb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nyanza","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lake (in Africa)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nyanza"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nyanza, Rwanda","blocks":[{"text":"Nyanza, also known as Nyabisindu, is a town located in Nyanza District in the Southern Province of Rwanda. Nyanza is the capital of the Southern Province."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/King%27s_palace_in_Nyanza.jpg/330px-King%27s_palace_in_Nyanza.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyanza%2C_Rwanda","wikidata":"Q528679"},{"title":"Nyanza District","blocks":[{"text":"Nyanza is a district in Southern Province, Republic of Rwanda. Its capital is Nyanza town, which is also the provincial capital. Nyanza is a Bantu word meaning lake, which probably refers to the small body of water created by a dam to the west of Nyanza town and sometimes referred to by the local residents as “Ikiyaga” or lake. which probably refers to a large lake to the west of Nyanza city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/NyanzaDist.png/330px-NyanzaDist.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyanza_District","wikidata":"Q2632821"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/King_Muzinga%E2%80%99s_dancers_in_Nyanza_1928._%289422840668%29.jpg/500px-King_Muzinga%E2%80%99s_dancers_in_Nyanza_1928._%289422840668%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/King_Muzinga%E2%80%99s_dancers_in_Nyanza_1928._%289422840668%29.jpg/1280px-King_Muzinga%E2%80%99s_dancers_in_Nyanza_1928._%289422840668%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.w